    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup hinges on two primary anchors today: **Corbin Carroll** (72.87) and **Mickey Moniak** (71.00). **Corbin Carroll** is our premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Wrobleski and a high-probability SB environment facilitated by the pitcher's slow delivery, which adds a 4% efficiency boost to his elite sprint profile. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** is in a smash spot against McGreevy, where a massive 14% platoon advantage significantly elevates his ceiling despite a neutral park environment. **Henry Bolte** also warrants attention; while his raw base projection is modest, his leadoff spot combined with the wind blowing out in the Miller, E matchup makes him a high-leverage start for our category targets.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Cole Young** on the bench. He posted a 42.59, narrowly missing the cut, but the optimizer prioritized the matchup volatility of **Josh Naylor** (44.08) and the structural necessity of keeping **Travis Bazzana** in the MI slot for his favorable platoon split. We are monitoring **Isaac Paredes** closely, as he remains \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have assumed a #3 spot for his projection, any move down the order could necessitate a pivot to **Cole Young** or **Zach McKinstry** if the bench were viable, though **Zach McKinstry** failed to clear our 40.0 floor today. \n\nWe are managing significant risk at the hot corner with **Austin Riley** (44.08). The matchup against Schlittler is a primary concern, as the pitcher's elite skill level (-19% to the score) effectively negates the benefit of **Austin Riley**\u2019s home park advantage. We are also monitoring the availability of **James Wood** and **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who remain sidelined on the IL. With the rest of our depth\u2014including **Jose Caballero**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Edwin Arroyo**\u2014holding at the ready, we are prioritizing high-efficiency matchups today to protect our game caps while aggressively chasing SB upside.",
